mothershipOS (mship.video): MMAP bitstream buffers. The decoder is the host's Venus through virtio-media, which can
only share virtio objects (e.g. virtio-gpu buffers) as DMABUFs; the client's linear blocks come from dmabuf heaps.
The input queue now uses the device's MMAP buffers and copies each bitstream chunk in (tens of KB per frame);
decoded frames still go straight into the client's gralloc buffers (DMABUF output queue).
ro.vendor.v4l2_codec2.input_mmap=false restores the DMABUF input queue.

